  "method": "Per edge compare old/new on identical next-day exposure targets and causal histories. Expected uniform random NDCG analytically conditions on each observed slate size n and positive count m: ((m/n)*sum(discount[1:min(k,n)]))/sum(discount[1:min(k,m)]), zero if m=0. Discount[i]=1/log2(i+1). Means weight requests equally, then releases equally. Oracle population mean is fraction of requests with m>0, due fixed all-negative=0. Relative change is 100*(current/parent-1), not percentage points and not compounded across different days. No new model inference or GPU use.",
